# TradingView parity exports stay OUT of the repo while it is public.
# NVDA and TSLA data is Nasdaq-licensed and TradingView's terms restrict
# redistribution, so committing it to a public repo is a licensing problem,
# not just an oversight. Put the exports here locally; they are read from disk
# and never committed. Reversed when the repo goes private (see OI-04, M1-13).
# Synthetic sample files are NOT licensed data and may be committed, which is
# how the loader and parity harness get something to test against in CI.
fixtures/parity/tradingview/*
!fixtures/parity/tradingview/.gitkeep
